 "stimulus_html": "For the following exercises, use the graphs from the given figures to determine whether the sequence of vertices in the given graph is a Hamilton cycle, an Euler circuit, both, or neither.\n<br>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/87a36cf2dd584f0d.png\" alt=\"Two graphs are labeled graph A and graph K. Graph A has five vertices: b, c, d, e, and f. Edges connect b c, c f, b d, b e, d e, and e f. Graph K has five vertices: m, n, o, p, and q. Edges connect m n, n o, n q, q o, o p, n p, and m p.\">\n\n<br>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/8b54c7fce19ca4a9.png\" alt=\"Graph F has five vertices. The vertices are a, b, c, d, and e. Edges connect a c, a b, e c, e b, c b, c d, and b d.\">\n",
